### PHASE 3 — Tournament Selection
Priority: MEDIUM | Risk: LOW
===========================================================================

Step 3.1 — Add to Population class in src/evolution.py (after crossover()):

    def tournament_select(self, k=3):
        candidates = random.sample(range(len(self.models)), k)
        best_idx = max(candidates, key=lambda i: self.fitnesses[i])
        return self.models[best_idx]

Step 3.2 — Replace inner while loop body in evolve() (keep elitism block):

    if random.random() < 0.10:
        parent = self.tournament_select(k=3)
        new_models.append(self.mutate(parent))
    else:
        parent1 = self.tournament_select(k=3)
        parent2 = self.tournament_select(k=3)
        child = self.crossover(parent1, parent2)
        child = self.mutate(child, in_place=True)
        new_models.append(child)

Step 3.3 — Verify:
  Run: python -c "from src.evolution import Population; p=Population(); p.fitnesses=[float(i) for i in range(50)]; p.evolve(); print('OK')"
  Expected: OK

DONE when: tournament_select added, evolve uses it, verify passes.

