## GEMINI EXECUTION RULES

1. Read before editing. Always view_file on the target before any edit.
   Never assume content from memory.

2. One phase at a time. Complete all steps and verification before advancing.

3. Commit at phase boundaries:
   git add -A && git commit -m "feat(phase-N): <phase title>"

4. No extra features. Add exactly what the step says. Ponytail principle:
   minimal code that works.

5. Crash = stop. Report exact error + traceback. Do not guess-fix.

6. Never commit .pth files to git. Check .gitignore.

7. Checkpoint deletion is safe and expected in Phases 4, 5, 6.

